    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0133" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President
                        Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d58-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-26">26 October 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Former Naval Person to President personal and most secret number 475 your number
                        396.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d58-f2"/></p>
                <p>1. I shall be delighted to meet you anywhere in North Africa, but I hope we need
                    not wait till the twentieth. Strongly recommend sea voyage to <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Anfa</hi> which we know, moving on to Pyramids if
                    and when convenient. By all means ask Chiang. If UJ refuses, then Molotov <pb
                        facs="0134" n="42" xml:id="pg42"/> with a Russian military mission would do.
                    It seems to me fine progress has been made by Hull and Eden at Moscow and still
                    more on the Russian southern front.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prime</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
